(2. A finite upper bound: no prime greater than 101) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Use Derickx--Stoll, arXiv:2505.14109v1, Theorem 3.3, Proposition 4.1,) Tj T*
(Remark 4.4, Proposition 5.2 and Corollary 7.5.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Oesterle gives p<=\(3^5+1\)^2=59536. For p>19 any modular point arising in) Tj T*
(degree 10 has exact degree 10: a smaller residue degree must divide 10,) Tj T*
(and S\(1\), S\(2\), S\(5\) contain no p>19.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For every prime 131<=p<=59536, Corollary 7.5 applies beyond its small-prime) Tj T*
(alternative because p^2>\(2^19/325\)*10+1. Its two exceptional CM possibilities) Tj T*
(would give p=21 or p=31. Otherwise it requires) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    \(p-1\)/\(2*str\(p\)\) | 10,) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(where str\(p\) is the lcm of the orders of strange characters and is 1 if) Tj T*
(there are none. The complete strange-character table makes this condition) Tj T*
(false for all 5987 primes in the indicated range. The script verify_bound.py) Tj T*
(checks the arithmetic against the saved table.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The remaining primes above 101 are 103,107,109,113,127. They are not strange,) Tj T*
(and 325*\(p^2-1\)/65536>50. Proposition 4.1 with a=2, ell=2, n=5 therefore makes) Tj T*
(the trace divisor invariant under <2>. Its orders in Delta\(p\) are respectively) Tj T*
(51,53,18,14,7. The possible geometric orbit lengths \(including elliptic-point) Tj T*
(ramification by 2 or 3\) never divide 10. An irreducible degree-10 point is) Tj T*
(therefore impossible. Remark 4.4 supplies the rational 2-torsion hypothesis.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. FRESH LOCAL CERTIFICATES IN DEGREE 10) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For p>37, a point arising over a degree-10 field has residue degree exactly) Tj T*
(10: smaller residue degrees divide 10 and are excluded by the known S\(1\),) Tj T*
(S\(2\),S\(5\). Let D be its irreducible trace divisor of degree 10.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The audit for S\(11\) recomputed the complete finite-field census through) Tj T*
(degree 11 and Hecke obstructions on the FULL modular curves for every) Tj T*
(prime 37<=p<=103. These calculations, rather than the conclusion about) Tj T*
(S\(11\), apply here. Their dependence on the total degree is checked below.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3a. Rational-cusp reductions) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The fresh degree-11 endomorphism certificates give the degree-10 formal) Tj T*
(immersion criterion as well. Normalize a degree-10 cusp multiplicity) Tj T*
(tuple so that its first entry is maximal, and add one to that entry.) Tj T*
(This is a degree-11 tuple included in the exhaustive successful check.) Tj T*
(The original ten Hecke operators are a subset of the eleven independent) Tj T*
(operators in that check, so they are independent. The endomorphisms used) Tj T*
(annihilate the rational Jacobian group independently of the degree.) Tj T*
(Thus the same formal immersion argument excludes every reduction of D) Tj T*
(supported on rational cusps. This uses the new index-20 combined map) Tj T*
(at 41 and the other fresh maps specified in the S\(11\) audit.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3b. Ordinary noncuspidal reductions) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At p>37 a degree-10 reduction has at most one ordinary noncuspidal closed) Tj T*
(point P. The minimum noncuspidal degree is at least 6 except at 41,) Tj T*
(where all degree-5 points are supersingular, there are no degree-6 or) Tj T*
(degree-7 points, and the minimum ordinary degree is 8. Its complementary cusps) Tj T*
(are rational. The fresh ordinary orbit counts through degree 10 are:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
