(All 96 orbits have non-principal alpha*A_3*P, certified by exact) Tj T*
(canonical-ring multiplication and independently checked full matrix) Tj T*
(ranks. The endomorphisms alpha are listed in Section 5 of the S\(11\)) Tj T*
(proof, including the stronger operators used at 97 and 101.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The obstruction applies to D of degree 10 without alteration. The class) Tj T*
(alpha[D-10c] is rational torsion; A_3 kills it, and A_3 kills the rational) Tj T*
(cusp complement. Therefore alpha*A_3*P would be principal. Its verified) Tj T*
(non-principality is a contradiction. The finite-image assertion for alpha,) Tj T*
(the target trace multiplicities, and the divisor obstruction do not use) Tj T*
(that the total degree is 11. In particular the former quotient-lifting) Tj T*
(issues at 97 and 101 are absent from this proof.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3c. Supersingular noncuspidal reductions) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The fresh census leaves three supersingular orbit types for p>37.) Tj T*
(At 41, degree 5, the native A_3 non-principality checks exclude a single) Tj T*
(closed point and every unordered pair, including repetition. These are) Tj T*
(the only possible multiple-noncuspidal-point reductions in degree 10.) Tj T*
(At 43, degree 7, the native alpha*A_3 check excludes the entire diamond) Tj T*
(orbit. Both calculations remain obstructions after adding rational cusps.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At 73, the supersingular points have degree 6 and are fixed as closed) Tj T*
(points by h=<2>, of order 9. Let C be the rational lift of the complementary) Tj T*
(cusp divisor, now of degree 4. The degree-zero class y=[h\(D-C\)-\(D-C\)] is rational torsion) Tj T*
(and reduces to zero. Hence 2y=0. The fresh exact JOne homology certificate) Tj T*
(shows that h acts trivially on rational 2-torsion, so the norm relation) Tj T*
(also gives 9y=0 and y=0. The gonality bound is greater than 26>10+4.) Tj T*
(It follows that hD+C=D+hC, hence hC=C. The free order-9 action on rational) Tj T*
(cusps would require 9|4, a contradiction.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Here is the torsion justification when Z=D-C does not have degree zero.) Tj T*
(If h has order m, put N_h Z=sum_\(i=0\)^\(m-1\) h^i Z. The divisor mZ-N_h Z) Tj T*
(has degree zero, and m[hZ-Z]=\(h-1\)[mZ-N_h Z]. Finiteness of \(h-1\)J\(Q\)) Tj T*
(therefore makes m[hZ-Z], and hence [hZ-Z] itself, torsion. This is the) Tj T*
(precise degree-zero interpretation used in all these stabilizer arguments.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3d. Nonrational cusp reductions) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Only p=41,43,73 have nonrational closed cusps of degree at most 10.) Tj T*
(At 41, either degree-10 cusp has non-principal A_3 image by the fresh) Tj T*
