() Tj T*
(At 43, a degree-7 cusp has a rational-cusp complement C of degree 3.) Tj T*
(The diamond h=<2>, of order 7, fixes that closed cusp. The fresh integral) Tj T*
(homology certificate shows trivial h-action on rational 2-torsion. As) Tj T*
(above, y=[h\(D-C\)-\(D-C\)] is killed by 2 and by the odd norm 7, so y=0.) Tj T*
(The NEW proved bound gon_Q X_1\(43\)>=16 is greater than 10+3=13. Thus) Tj T*
(hD+C=D+hC, which would require 7|3. This supplies the gonality bound) Tj T*
(needed here without assuming the stronger website bound quoted in the) Tj T*
(earlier writeup.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At 73, the nonrational cusps have degree 9, with rational complement C) Tj T*
(of degree 1. The order-9 diamond h=<2> fixes the closed cusp; its action) Tj T*
(on rational 2-torsion is trivial. The norm and gonality arguments would) Tj T*
(require 9|1. There are no other cuspidal cases.) Tj T*
